ants /Library/Keychains read+write to any com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension holder, and 655-656 grant the securityd Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No value, no portal capability, no new App ID, no C1 change. FIELD-BY-FIELD (all five keys on the row): status prohibited-pending-decision -> prohibited; rationale -> the settled reason above citing TASK-260728-7ii1xz; evidence -> keep and add application.sb:792-793 plus checks E8-E10; resolutionOwner -> REMOVE (this task IS the resolution; a settled row naming a pending resolver reads as still-open); amendmentRule -> REMOVE and replace with M5. The amendmentRule removal is the critical one: its antecedent (transport gives the provider direct keychain access) is now TRUE while its consequent (amend to required with the group literal) is FALSE, so left in place it is a live instruction to re-grant the row on exactly the reasoning this decision refutes. M2: close OC-1 naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz as resolver. M3: keep OC-4 open, downgraded to verify-only-if-XPC-is-ever-selected. M4: macos.host keychain-access-groups - no change requested, recommend keep granted with the purpose narrowed to iOS system of record plus a macOS pre-seed staging item. M5: record the replacement rule - on macOS the file-based keychain is SecAccess-ACL controlled and keychain-access-groups applies only to the Data Protection Keychain, so a root-context provider never needs it and the presence of the key in a shipping third-party provider is not evidence it functions; the row reopens only if the provider is ever moved into a user context. M6: application-groups on both macOS targets - no value change, but the stated purpose and the section 10 traceability row implying a shared container on macOS are FALSE (host and provider resolve different containers). M7: bump revision, append a revisionLog entry naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz_reviewer-verdict-01.md and this decision, keep validate-matrix at exit 0, and check that deleting resolutionOwner/amendmentRule does not trip an exhaustive containment assertion - if one requires them it encoded the open state and must be updated in the same revision. Consider a negative gate: a prohibited row still carrying a resolutionOwner is a contradiction. See TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md section 7.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-d6c87d, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-d6c87d)\nr4 rework against reviewer verdict 03 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1 plus a secondary correction), and application of the TASK-260728-7ii1xz r2 amendment packet M1-M7 in the same revision because M1 and F1 touch the same two rows. F1 independently CONFIRMED against the r3 artifact. Neither of the reviewer two exits applied verbatim: 7ii1xz finished in the interim and its M6 explicitly handed the least-privilege call to this task, so the survey was done rather than the row deferred again. Verdict: com.apple.security.application-groups is PROHIBITED on all four macOS targets (production AND probe) and required on all four iOS targets - new rule G4. Basis is a grant-by-grant read of /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb 26.5/25F71 at lines 302-330 and 459-465, the only two places the key appears: six grants, three home-relative and broken across the root/user split, three system-wide and belonging to mechanisms this project does not use (Mac App Store group content, a group-prefixed XPC Mach service which 7ii1xz rejected as candidate C, group-prefixed POSIX IPC which nobody proposed). M6 open question about a private root-context container is answered harder than M6 expected: appsandbox-container-common and -macos at application.sb:107-108 are unconditional, so every sandboxed target already has its own container and a group container adds only sharing, which is exactly what is broken. Ceremony C1 shrank - no App Group record, no App Groups capability on any App ID - and the convenience argument evaporates rather than being demoted, because C1 already excludes all four iOS App IDs under ADR-024 and those are the records only consumers. Amendment packet applied in full: M1 all five fields including deletion of resolutionOwner and amendmentRule, M2 OC-1 closed, M3 OC-4 dormant plus new sandbox-side evidence that the Mach prefix mechanism is style-agnostic, M4 macos.host purpose narrowed as recommended, M5 rule K1, M6, M7. M7 warning checked and did not bite - the containment assertions key off status, not row metadata. Beyond the literal ask, two things stated in the handoff: the macOS PROBE rows were withheld too (leaving them would park the identical defect one row over), and the amendment packet was applied in the same revision. Secondary correction fixed and the number moved underneath it: the macos.host development allowlist is nine keys, not seven or ten, because the App Group is no longer authored. Gates: reviewer own targeted jq gate true/exit 0 (was false/exit 1); validate_matrix.py 30 rules 801 checks exit 0; mutate.py 66/66 negative gates exit 0 including one that rejects the over-correction; 15/15 r3 preservation assertions hold; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. Both harness scripts re-verified running in place from the board resource layout. Recorded not actioned: PlatformVPNIdentity.appGroupIdentifier is unsatisfiable on macOS (owner TASK-260715-1tzaed) and .spec/architecture.md:111 needs amendment. No board element created or changed; no product source, spec, or generated project modified.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-d6c87d, pid=90126, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-cca63d, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-cca63d)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-cca63d, pid=99219, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-e5df4d, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-e5df4d)\nr5 (2026-07-28.r5) closes all three verdict-04 findings. F1: keychain-access-groups prohibited on macos.host and therefore all four macOS targets, new rule K2 (sharing needs a named second member; the injected app-identifier supplies the host default group) — plus the moved-default-group consequence recorded for TASK-260715-379cpk. F3: application-groups prohibited on both iOS probe rows (TASK-260715-1jckn0 names no shared container), G4 gains probeRule, and the consumerless probe App Group record is deleted; G3 restated. F2: TASK-260728-q5kjta scope+AC4 corrected on the board to match c1AuthorizationScope. Gates: 846 checks exit 0, 92/92 negative gates, 32/32 r4 preservation assertions, legacy+board validate+swift test (335) all exit 0. Both reviewer jq gates flipped to true/exit 0. Ready for review.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-e5df4d, pid=6997, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-f8c481, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-f8c481)\nReviewer verdict 05 (2026-07-28): CHANGES REQUESTED, routed to analysis. F1: authoritative r5 JSON crossPlatformRules[2] still grants the shared Keychain group to macos.host while target rows, K2, consumers, A6, and A17 prohibit it; independent gate false/exit 1 and the 846-check validator misses this projection. F2: portal consumer TASK-260715-3jloqy still instructs shared-group/App Group/Keychain capability creation and provider-only packet-tunnel authorization, contradicting r5/C1 (four macOS App IDs, Network Extensions on hosts and providers, zero App Group/Keychain portal mutation); query exit 0, consistency gate false/exit 1. Evidence: TASK-260715-ypo7yo_reviewer-verdict-05.md. Other gates: validator 846/exit 0; mutations 92/92 exit 0; swift test 335/335 exit 0; legacy guard exit 0; board validate exit 0. Recoverable autonomous metadata/contract rework; no external decision.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-f8c481, pid=23352, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-6b2f1c, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-6b2f1c)\nr6 rework against reviewer verdict 05 (CHANGES REQUESTED, F1 + F2). Both findings independently re-verified before acceptance and both CONFIRMED. No entitlement decision changed and no target row moved - both are cases of a statement about the contract contradicting the contract. F1: the reviewer jq gate was re-run against r5 (false/exit 1) and the finding was then widened - a sweep of every string in the r5 JSON found a SECOND stale claim the reviewer had not named (appGroupStyleRule per family, true of r4 two records, false since r5 deleted the probe record). So the class is closed rather than the string patched: new rule S1 (crossPlatformSharingContract) gives every cross-platform sentence a structured rule, R32 derives each grant set from the target rows, cross-checks it against the record own consumedByTargets, then requires the grantClause verbatim, the names inside it to equal the derived set, and every other target named in the sentence to be a declared non-grantee mention with its own clause; R33 requires the same clauses in the rationale document so the two artifacts cannot drift; and a count scan requires any App Group record-count claim to sit at a registered path and match the record list. The count scan failed on its first run on appGroupLeastPrivilegeRule - a THIRD stale claim (r4 two records) that neither the reviewer nor r5 had spotted - now fixed. One deliberate divergence from the literal rework text, stated in the JSON as whyTheMacOSHostIsNotNamed: the corrected sentence excludes macOS universally instead of naming the macOS host, because naming a target is exactly what went stale; the reviewer own textual gate passes. F2: TASK-260715-3jloqy description, scope, AC and checklist corrected on the board to c1AuthorizationScope exactly, pinned in the JSON as rule P1, and gated by the new TASK-260715-ypo7yo_check-portal-consumer.py which reproduces the reviewer hand check (14 failures over 20 checks before the fix, exit 0 after). The removed AC2 clause packet-tunnel entitlement only on provider identifiers contradicted r1, not just r5: R7 has required the entitlement on all eight target rows since r2, so provider-only verification would have passed a portal state in which neither macOS host App ID carries the capability. Gates: reviewer jq gate true/exit 0 (was false/exit 1); validate_matrix.py 33 rules 975 checks exit 0; mutate.py 117/117 negative gates exit 0 including two that mutate the rationale document; 53/53 r5 preservation assertions hold; board gate exit 0; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. All harnesses re-verified running in place from the board resource layout. Two blank exit codes in the first transcript pass came from bash-only PIPESTATUS under zsh; both commands were re-run without a pipeline and both exited 0, recorded in the log rather than smoothed over. No board element created, deleted or re-parented; no product source, spec or generated project modified. Ready for review.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-6b2f1c, pid=25888, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-26c930, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-26c930)\nReviewer verdict 06: changes requested. Authoritative matrix is r6, but Ceremony C1 task TASK-260728-q5kjta still authorizes rejected/superseded r5; independent freshness gate false, exit 1. Full evidence: TASK-260715-ypo7yo_reviewer-verdict-06.md. Route: analysis.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-26c930, pid=43067, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-36bfba, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-36bfba)\nr7 rework against reviewer verdict 06 (CHANGES REQUESTED). The single blocking finding F1 was independently re-verified before being accepted: the reviewer's jq freshness gate re-run verbatim against r6 returned false/exit 1, and the C1 record's mutation set was then checked field by field against c1AuthorizationScope independently of the reviewer's claim that it matched - all four authorized App IDs present with a right boundary, Network Extensions and Mac Development wording present, ADR-024 cited, all four iOS App IDs and works.relux.proxy only inside a negation. CONFIRMED, and the revision label was the only defect, so the mutation set is preserved byte-for-byte. The class was then swept rather than assumed bounded: all 402 live board elements scanned for a matrix revision label, finding exactly two - q5kjta.scope (the finding) and this task's own notes field, which the reviewer did not report and which is NOT a defect because notes is append-only history; that distinction is why rule A1's boardGate declares excludedFields. All four required rework items done: q5kjta.scope re-pointed r5 -> r7 (character delta 0, mutation set untouched); the board gate extended from one live consumer to both, with the authorization-node check requiring the current revision and the exact c1AuthorizationScope; 13 board-record negative gates added, including the r6 defect verbatim; the stale check-portal-consumer.sh reference corrected in the rationale AND in the validator docstring, which carried the same stale name. The digest alternative the verdict offered is rejected with reasoning recorded in the contract. The class is closed by rule A1 plus a derived banned-revision set plus amendmentRule now requiring every amendment to re-point both pinned consumers, which R34 enforces - that omission was the actual root cause. The new negative gates found two defects in the gates themselves: the r6 right-boundary regex could not see a sentence-final identifier, and a 220-char negation window let an adjacent clause's NOT launder an authorization; both fixed, and negationWindow was removed rather than left vestigial. Gates: validate_matrix.py 1024 checks exit 0; mutate.py 130/130 exit 0; preserve.py 57 assertions exit 0; check-portal-consumer.py 43 checks over 2 consumers exit 0; reviewer jq gate true exit 0; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. All three harnesses verified to run in place from the board resource layout. One board field changed on one element: TASK-260728-q5kjta.scope. No board element created, deleted, re-parented or re-linked. No portal mutation, no product source, spec file or generated project touched.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-36bfba, pid=45795, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_syst